A typeahead search can show stale results. Current code:
```javascript
let lastQuery = '';
async function search(q) {
  lastQuery = q;
  const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);
  const results = await res.json();
  render(results);
}
```
Users type fast: request for "car" resolves first, then slower request for "cat" resolves and overwrites UI. Which change prevents stale results without modifying the API?

options:
```javascript
let lastQuery = '';
async function search(q) {
  lastQuery = q;
  const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);
  const results = await res.json();
  if (q !== lastQuery) return; // skip stale response
  render(results);
}
```

```javascript
async function search(q) {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);
  requestAnimationFrame(() => render(res.json()));
}
```

```javascript
async function search(q) {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`, { cache: 'no-store' });
  render(await res.json());
}
```

```javascript
async function search(q) {
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 0));
  const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);
  render(await res.json());
}
```

