After redeploys, users still see old titles, and Google shows stale snippets. What’s the correct fix to keep assets fast but HTML fresh?

options:
Load GA4 in the head with async, set default consent denied, then update consent and manually send page_view on accept.

```html
<!-- head -->
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-XXXX"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag('consent', 'default', { 'analytics_storage': 'denied' });
  gtag('js', new Date());
  gtag('config', 'G-XXXX', { 'send_page_view': false });
</script>
<!-- on consent -->
<script>
  gtag('consent', 'update', { 'analytics_storage': 'granted' });
  gtag('event', 'page_view');
</script>
```

